		(uuid "233ed2ab-776c-4406-be44-b04a0d24a9ae")
	)
	(text "Core assumptions\n\nPower: 2S → LMR33630 → 3V3 rail.\n\nVBAT sense: 27 k (top) / 10 k (bottom) to ADC with 100 nF at the MCU pin.\n\nOutput to ELRS (now): PPM.\n\nHaptic motor and magnetic buzzer: low-side MOSFET (IRLML0030), SS14 flyback across load (cathode to +3V3, anode to switch node).\n\nAvoid D0/D1 for anything (keep for Serial/bootloader).\n\nRecommended pinout (I²C OLED version – simplest, no conflicts)\n\nELRS / control\n\nD9 → PPM_OUT to ELRS GPIO13 (100 Ω series).\n\nOptional future CRSF: break out a 4-pin header 3V3 / GND / UART_TX / UART_RX from any spare USART; wire later in firmware.\n\nJoysticks (KY-023)\n\nA0 → Right X (Roll) — wiper via 1 k, 100 nF to GND at pin\n\nA1 → Right Y (Pitch) — wiper via 1 k, 100 nF\n\nA2 → Left X (Yaw) — wiper via 1 k, 100 nF\n\nA3 → Left Y (Throttle) — wiper via 1 k, 100 nF\n\nEach stick’s +V to 3V3, GND to GND. Stick push-switches are optional; you already have 4 buttons below.\n\nSwitches (momentary PTS647) – to GND, use INPUT_PULLUP\n\nD7 → SW1 (Arm)\n\nD8 → SW2 (Mode)\n\nD10 → SW3 (OK/Enter)\n\nD4 → SW4 (Back)\n\nIndicators / actuators\n\nD5 → LED1\n\nD6 → LED2\n\nD2 → Buzzer MOSFET gate (100–220 Ω series, 100 k pulldown). Buzzer + to 3V3, – to MOSFET drain. SS14 across buzzer: cathode to 3V3, anode to drain.\n\nD3 → Haptic MOSFET gate (same gate network). ERM + to 3V3, – to drain. SS14 across ERM: cathode to 3V3, anode to drain.\n\nVBAT measurement\n\nA7 → VBAT divider node (27 k top to VBAT, 10 k bottom to GND), 100 nF from A7 to GND at the pin.\n\nDisplay connector (your 6-pin, set to 3.3 V) – I²C mode\n\nPin-1: 3V3\n\nPin-2: GND\n\nPin-3: SCL → A5\n\nPin-4: SDA → A4\n\nPin-5: NC (MISO not used on I²C)\n\nPin-6: NC (CS not used on I²C)\n\nThis version keeps SPI pins free and leaves you maximum headroom.\n\nAlternative pinout changes if you choose SPI TFT (ST7735/ST7789)\n\nKeep everything above unchanged except the display and two switch pins:\n\nSPI signals (use the MCU’s hardware SPI pins)\n\nConnector Pin-3 SCK → SCK (ICSP SCK / board SCK pin)\n\nConnector Pin-4 MOSI → MOSI (ICSP MOSI / board MOSI pin)\n\nConnector Pin-5 MISO → MISO (if your TFT uses it; otherwise NC)\n\nConnector Pin-6 CS → D10 (dedicated CS)\n\nAdd two control lines for SPI displays\n\nD2 → DC (data/command)\n\nD3 → RST\n\nBecause D2/D3 are now used for DC/RST, move the two buttons that were on D2/D3 in the I²C plan as follows:\n\nSW3 (OK/Enter) stays on D10 only if you are on I²C.\nFor SPI, dedicate D10 to CS and move SW3 to D12 (works fine; not used if your TFT doesn’t need MISO).\n\nSW4 (Back) remains D4.\n\nSummary (SPI):\n\nD10 = CS (no switch here)\n\nD2 = DC\n\nD3 = RST\n\nIf your TFT needs MISO, keep D12 for MISO and place SW3 on another free pin (e.g., D14/D15 if available on your board).\n\nIf you want me to lock this to the exact Nano-Every Arduino pin labels for the SPI block (ICSP header vs D11–D13), say which footprint you’re using and I’ll pin it precisely.\n\nNotes you’ll want during bring-up\n\nVBAT maths (27k:10k): scale = (27+10)/10 = 3.7.\nVbat = adc * (Vref/1023) * 3.7. With 8.4 V full → ≈2.27 V at A7.\nDo a dummy read after mux change and average 8–16 samples.\n\nPPM: D9 is the canonical output used by many Arduino PPM encoders; keep the wire short to the ELRS GPIO13. Configure ELRS firmware for PPM input on GPIO13.\n\nFlyback diodes: SS14 across magnetic buzzer and ERM motor only (cathode to 3V3, anode to switch node). No diode on a piezo.\n\nMOSFET gates: 100–220 Ω series, 100 k pulldown to GND. Keep loop area small (place diode close to load/MOSFET)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
