	(text "from my experience\nstandard via drill size >= 0.3/0.4mm\nless layer count, 4 is the sweet spot\nstick to common and easy-to-solder packaging (qfp/qfn, 0402 min, no bga)\nsurface finish, hasl leaded is the cheapest in most fab\npanelize boards for higher quantity\nsingle sided assembly\noptimize bom - consolidate diff component values (i.e. 2x 1k when 1k is already used elsewhere vs. 2k and 1k)\njlc specific\nmaximize their basic parts library in ur bom\nuse their economic assembly\nOsiris\n\n — Yesterday at 17:28\nBut that could result in less well designed PCBs.\nI personally wouldn't fly a 4 layer FC\nThat most likely would result in frequently corner cutting with regard to PCB best practices\nemrick — Yesterday at 17:29\nfor 6 layers, is S-G-S-P-G-S good for FC?\nOsiris\n\n — Yesterday at 17:29\n(unless the FC is huge)\nOsiris\n\n — Yesterday at 17:30\nyou could use the power plane as return path yes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -279.146 -353.314 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8cd20df8-f0e7-4b0a-bb6a-941cfc727a16")
	)
