	(text "IFOUT — Analog Out. 480 MHz IF output from the mixer/IF front-end; normally routed out to an external SAW band-pass filter and back into IFIN. \nopendevices.ru\n\nIFIN — Analog In. Return from the SAW filter into the chip’s IF amplifier/demod chain. Keep the IFOUT–SAW–IFIN path very short/controlled. \nopendevices.ru\n\nBBOUT2 — Analog Out. FM video baseband (demod) buffer output. Typically AC-coupled and fed to the internal video amp input (VAMPIN), with optional external RC shaping. \nopendevices.ru\n\nVAMPIN — Analog In. Video amplifier input (takes the demodulated video from BBOUT2). \nopendevices.ru\n\nVAMPOUT — Analog Out. Video amplifier output; drive your CVBS output here (AC-couple and terminate for ~1 Vpp into 75 Ω). \nopendevices.ru\n\nFMIN_65 — Analog In. 6.5 MHz audio subcarrier input to the audio demod path; normally taken from the video baseband via a 6.5 MHz ceramic band-pass filter placed between FMIN_65 and AUIN_65. \nopendevices.ru\n+1\n\nAUIN_65 — Analog In. Input to the 6.5 MHz audio demod/amp after the ceramic filter. \nopendevices.ru\n\nAUOUT_65 — Analog Out. Demodulated audio output from the 6.5 MHz path (line-level; AC-couple). \nopendevices.ru\n\nVT_65 — Analog Out. 6.5 MHz audio demodulator VCO/PLL loop node (“audio demod out” in table). You add the small RC loop-filter network here; community docs show a working network (e.g., ~200 Ω/430 k/470 pF/100 pF + 4.7 µF). \nopendevices.ru\n+1\n\nAGC_C — Analog I/O. AGC rectifier/output node for the IF chain; decouple with a capacitor to set AGC dynamics. You can also monitor it as an AGC indicator. (For a calibrated strength output, use RSSI pin IFPDC_C.)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 2153.92 -601.472 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "bc60dfb1-ab92-4db0-adc3-1f1dfe344483")
	)
